{"content":"Found and fixed the root cause. In sqlparse/sql.py, TokenList.flatten() had its branches inverted: it was yielding the group token itself (without recursing) when a token was a group, and only recursing (no-op) for leaf tokens. This meant nested group tokens' cached `.value` (set once at construction time) was used in `__str__`/serialization instead of being recomputed from children, so any in-place modification of nested group contents (like StripCommentsFilter removing a comment inside an Identifier group) was invisible to the rendered output.

Swapped the branches so flatten() recurses into groups (yield from token.flatten()) and yields leaf tokens directly (yield token). This correctly flattens the full token tree so __str__ picks up post-processing changes to nested tokens.

Verified with a manual repro script (dbg.py) that `sqlparse.format('select * from foo -- comment\nwhere', strip_comments=True)` now correctly returns `'select * from foo \nwhere'` instead of the stale pre-strip value. Now running the full test suite to confirm no regressions, then will remove the temporary debug script.","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_1","name":"run","arguments":{"command":"python -m pytest --no-header -q","timeout_seconds":300}}]}
